                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "3/10 Zombie Pirates is a minimal tower defense game where you fight against zombies in pirate ships. Clunky, ugly, and deeply flawed.\n\nZombie Pirates is an extremely below average tower defense game. Place pirate ships with varying combat abilities fighting against zombies in pirate ships. There’s an overarching storyline to follow while playing but it isn’t the main center of the game and isn’t implemented very well, if you’re paying attention I feel like we’re the bad guys. I didn’t encounter any bugs while playing.\n\nI couldn’t get myself to play more than ten minutes of this title. The art style wasn’t for me and the mechanics were very clunky with minimal world building or unique differences from other tower defense games to keep me playing. For example, a lot of the gameplay is close range but there isn’t any way to dodge oncoming attacks so it becomes a free for all once you get close enough to the zombie ships. Everything felt very repetitive and clunky including the sound effects and music used.\n\nNo achievements.\n\n[u]Pros[/u]\n[list]\n   [*] There is a story albeit not a great one.\n   [*] Didn’t encounter any bugs.\n[/list]\n\n[u]Cons[/u]\n[list]\n   [*] The story.\n   [*] Extremely clunky gameplay. \n   [*] Repetitive.\n   [*] Run-Of-The-Mill tower defense game.\n   [*] Average sound effects and music choices.\n   [*] No achievements.\n   [*] Frustrating.\n [/list]\n\nTo see more reviews like this one, support me by following my curating page:\nhttps://store.steampowered.com/curator/46085490-SumiSux-At-Games/\n",
